# No Rounded-Corner Squares Behind Icons

Icons in this app must **NEVER** be placed on top of a rounded-corner square
(or any square/rectangular badge/tile/chip) background. Render the icon on its
own, with no boxed backdrop behind it. This is a permanent, non-negotiable design rule.

This applies to all icons everywhere: nav items, buttons, list rows, cards,
feature callouts, status indicators, empty states, etc.

## What is banned

- A `<div>`/`<span>` wrapper around an icon that has both a background
  (`background`, `background-color`, gradient, etc.) AND `border-radius`.
- Utility combos like `rounded-*` + `bg-*` on an icon container.
- "Icon tile" / "icon badge" / "icon chip" patterns.

## Examples

```html
<!-- ❌ BAD: icon sits on a rounded-corner square -->
<div style="width:40px;height:40px;border-radius:12px;background:#eef;">
  <svg class="icon">...</svg>
</div>

<!-- ❌ BAD: same thing with utility classes -->
<span class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-indigo-100 flex items-center justify-center">
  <i class="icon"></i>
</span>

<!-- ✅ GOOD: bare icon, no boxed backdrop -->
<svg class="icon">...</svg>

<!-- ✅ GOOD: icon in a fully round container (circle) is allowed -->
<span class="icon-avatar" style="border-radius:50%;">
  <svg class="icon">...</svg>
</span>
```

## Rules for the agent

- Never generate a rounded-square/tile/badge background behind an icon.
- When editing or copying existing markup, strip any such wrapper you touch.
- If a container is needed, use a fully circular container (`border-radius: 50%`)
  or no background at all — never a rounded rectangle.
